+## SELECTPAGE01: selected grouped bitmap record pages (2026-09-26)
+
+Official PostgreSQL 18 index locking and generic WAL contracts re-read:
+https://www.postgresql.org/docs/18/index-locking.html and
+https://www.postgresql.org/docs/18/generic-wal.html. The indexed read still uses
+the existing PageStore/PG buffer-manager path. No FFI, buffer lock, WAL write,
+on-disk format, snapshot, or heap visibility boundary changes. The access
+method remains responsible for concurrent index changes; a bitmap index scan
+is only used with a qualifying MVCC snapshot under PostgreSQL's contract.
+
+The catalog descriptor identifies up to three physical pages per bitmap. The
+first page contains the complete header and directory. The reader validates
+that directory, key, kind, page mask, and every fetched physical page identity,
+extent, length, and following intra-record link. It then fetches only extents
+that contain candidate heap-page offsets. Unvisited payloads are neither read
+nor validated, matching Bitmap::open's established lazy offset contract.
+Build verification still reads and validates complete records. Every returned
+offset is decoded and checked before candidate emission.
+
+The in-memory exact-row test creates two liveness and two posting record pages,
+then proves a selective AND reads one of each. The grouped oracle and native
+SQL lifecycle/CPU qualification are separate gates. Native evidence and final
+review status will be recorded with the tested module revision.
+
 Review: the same live relation and full-CAPACITY exclusive extent prove the
 relocated FFI call. New oracle tests compare fresh/reloaded images across kinds,
 assert stable buffer address, exercise failures/recovery and preserve zero tails.
